Changes from tincan 0.9.2, made by Reason Machines:
- The binary is named reason-network and agents see it as "reason-network": the MCP server
  name and serverInfo, the opencode plugin and pi extension files, the Copilot CLI hook
  file, Gemini CLI hook names, message tags and user-facing text.
- `setup` removes the wiring and login service an earlier build of the same binary
  installed under the name "tincan", and installs its service as com.reasonmachines.network.
- Settings are read from REASON_NETWORK_* environment variables, falling back to TINCAN_*.
- The daemon never updates itself; the Reason CLI installs a pinned, checksum-verified build.
The network protocol, invite format and data directory are unchanged, so it interoperates
with tincan 0.9.x peers.
